Actually, for durations (r, g, y), the green interval is at offset r in each repeating cycle of length r + g + y. The number of overlaps is therefore the count of t from 0 to n - 1 such that t mod (r_a + g_a + y_a) == r_a and t mod (r_b + g_b + y_b) == r_b. The loop shown in the example does that count correctly.

